      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-240536",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/07/070aeb7370e7e254b4019d984914871dbbc3a75d901064b656950a7065614ca2.png)\n\nIn the diagram above, the parallel lines $AB^(\u27f7)$ and $CD^(\u27f7)$ are crossed by the transversal $PQ^(\u27f7)$.\n\nConsider the following statement:\n\n> *$\u2220CSQ$ and $\u2220ARP$ are supplementary.*\n\nThe table below gives the proof of the statement. Select the correct options in the table and thus complete the proof.\n\n|  | Statement | Reason |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| 1 | {{field-1}} | Linear pair postulate |\n| 2 | $m\u2220ARS + m\u2220ARP = 180^{\u2218}$ | {{field-2}} |\n| 3 | $\u2220ARS\u2245\u2220CSQ$ | {{field-3}} |\n| 4 | $m\u2220ARS = m\u2220CSQ$ | Definition of congruent angles |\n| 5 | $m\u2220CSQ + m\u2220ARP = 180^{\u2218}$ | Substitution |\n| 6 | $\u2220CSQ$ and $\u2220ARP$ are supplementary | Definition of supplementary angles |"
    }
